  "note": "Triennial election of the 19 electoral divisions of Dungannon rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Twelve Unionists and five Nationalists were returned unopposed; Crossdernott and Coalisland were contested. The new council had thirteen Unionists and six Nationalists, with three members to be co-opted. Three Nationalists nominated for the seat vacated by John O'Neill (Lab.), who did not seek re-election. All three names and figures are on the cited page (the OCR reads Cullen as Cullcn), and in the Mid-Ulster Mail, 14 June 1952, p. 6."
